I can sing in creative.
我能用角色的声音唱。

297
00:12:57.120 --> 00:12:59.040
Clearly, this is a pet peeve of mine.
很明显，这是我的一个心病。

298
00:12:59.280 --> 00:12:59.920
Pet peeve.
心病。

299
00:13:00.400 --> 00:13:02.920
Warning, if you sing happy birthday around Jenna.
警告，如果你在珍娜身边唱《生日快乐歌》的话。

300
00:13:04.200 --> 00:13:06.200
I can sing if I'm doing a character.
如果我在扮演某个角色，我就能唱。

301
00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:11.400
And also there's some songs from church that I feel like I can carry the tune just because
还有一些教堂里的歌，我觉得我能唱准调，纯粹是因为

302
00:13:11.400 --> 00:13:12.680
I've sung them so many times.
我唱过太多遍了。

303
00:13:12.860 --> 00:13:14.740
My favorite part of church was the singing.
我去教堂最喜欢的部分就是唱歌。

304
00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:15.200
Yeah.
是啊。

305
00:13:15.380 --> 00:13:16.400
And I would sing out.
我会放声高歌。

306
00:13:16.600 --> 00:13:17.100
Me too.
我也是。

307
00:13:17.360 --> 00:13:21.880
And he will raise you up on eagle's wings.
他会用鹰的翅膀将你托起。

308
00:13:22.140 --> 00:13:22.540
Yes.
没错。

309
00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:23.020
Yeah.
是啊。

310
00:13:23.260 --> 00:13:24.080
There was a song.
有那么一首歌。

311
00:13:24.220 --> 00:13:25.900
Of course, you know, my family is like Southern.
当然，你知道的，我的家庭属于南方派。

312
00:13:26.440 --> 00:13:28.120
I would belt out so hard.
我会唱得特别卖力。

313
00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:29.640
And it was at Easter.
那是在复活节的时候。

314
00:13:29.640 --> 00:13:34.040
And it would be like, there ain't no grave gonna hold my body down.
歌词大概是，没有任何坟墓能困住我的身体。

315
00:13:34.700 --> 00:13:35.060
Yeah.
没错。

316
00:13:35.240 --> 00:13:36.440
And it's about the resurrection.
那是关于复活的。

317
00:13:37.720 --> 00:13:39.380
And I went for it.
我当时完全投入进去了。

318
00:13:39.760 --> 00:13:41.920
We were at church recently when I went back home.
最近我回老家时去了趟教堂。

319
00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:43.380
And I started to belt out a song.
我开始放声高歌。

320
00:13:43.500 --> 00:13:45.220
And my daughter looked at me like, what?
我女儿看着我，那眼神仿佛在说，怎么了？

321
00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:47.440
Can you dial down the volume?
你能小点声吗？

322
00:13:47.820 --> 00:13:49.560
I mean, most of church is boring.
我是说，大部分教堂礼拜都很无聊。

323
00:13:49.740 --> 00:13:50.620
Let's be honeSt.
说实话吧。

324
00:13:50.880 --> 00:13:52.220
Jenna, it is.
珍娜，确实如此。

325
00:13:52.500 --> 00:13:53.140
Come on.
得了吧。

326
00:13:53.320 --> 00:13:55.040
Why can't I say stuff we all know?
为什么我不能说出大家都知道的事实呢？

327
00:13:55.280 --> 00:13:55.960
You can.
你可以说。

328
00:13:56.080 --> 00:13:56.720
And you do.
而且你确实说了。

329
00:13:56.720 --> 00:13:58.220
I'm gonna be 50.
我就要50岁了。

330
00:13:58.540 --> 00:13:59.900
I'm moments away from 50.
离50岁就差那么一点点了。

331
00:14:00.040 --> 00:14:01.140
And it's all coming out.
所以一切都藏不住了。

332
00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:01.980
It's all coming out.
全都藏不住了。

333
00:14:05.800 --> 00:14:08.900
Well, are we gonna take a break and then get into this episode?
那么，我们要先休息一下再开始这集的内容吗？

334
00:14:08.900 --> 00:14:09.520
Or what are we doing?
还是说我们现在要做什么？

335
00:14:09.760 --> 00:14:10.820
Let's take a break.
休息一下吧。

336
00:14:11.020 --> 00:14:12.380
Let's take a break.
休息一下吧。

337
00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:16.360
Break me off a piece of that podcast show.
给我来一小段播客节目吧。

338
00:14:18.160 --> 00:14:30.500
We are back.
我们回来了。

339
00:14:30.660 --> 00:14:34.880
And before we start breaking down this episode, I've got some tidbits from the call sheet.
在开始拆解这一集之前，我从通告单上找了一些花絮。

340
00:14:35.040 --> 00:14:35.740
Oh, yeah?
哦，是吗？

341
00:14:36.080 --> 00:14:37.380
Thanks to Steve Burgess.
多亏了史蒂夫·伯吉斯。

342
00:14:37.380 --> 00:14:42.180
We started filming this episode on Monday, September 10th, 2012.
我们是在2012年9月10日星期一开拍这一集的。

343
00:14:42.680 --> 00:14:46.600
Are you curious what we filmed on that very first day of Here Comes Trouble?
你好奇我们在《麻烦来了》第一天拍了什么吗？

344
00:14:47.140 --> 00:14:47.700
Yes.
好奇。

345
00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:48.360
Good.
很好。

346
00:14:48.500 --> 00:14:49.560
I hope you are.
希望你好奇。

347
00:14:49.820 --> 00:14:53.680
Because I'm gonna tell you, it was all talking heads.
因为我要告诉你，那天拍的全是访谈镜头。

348
00:14:53.860 --> 00:14:58.980
All morning, all the talking heads you see in the episode, we were filming on the first day.
整个上午，你在这一集里看到的所有访谈镜头，我们都是在第一天拍的。

349
00:14:58.980 --> 00:15:04.340
And then towards the end of the day, we did have two big group scenes in the bullpen.
然后在一天快结束的时候，我们在办公区拍了两场大型群戏。

350
00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:08.840
And it was a very, very busy production week for our show.
那对我们剧组来说是非常、非常忙碌的一周。

351
00:15:09.060 --> 00:15:11.880
They were prepping the farm and the boat.
他们当时正在筹备农场和船的拍摄场景。

352
00:15:12.260 --> 00:15:14.980
There was a dirt test for the farm.
农场那边做了一个土壤测试。

353
00:15:15.540 --> 00:15:18.340
So, someone was getting dirt thrown in their face.
所以，有人被弄了一脸泥。

354
00:15:18.460 --> 00:15:18.640
Yeah.
是啊。

355
00:15:19.040 --> 00:15:20.380
To see how it would look.
为了看看效果如何。

356
00:15:20.500 --> 00:15:22.400
They were scouting locations for the boat.
他们当时正在为船寻找外景地。

357
00:15:22.580 --> 00:15:28.040
We had an NBC EPK crew doing interviews with all the cast this week.
这周NBC的EPK摄制组来给所有演员做了采访。

358
00:15:28.040 --> 00:15:28.720
Yes.
没错。

359
00:15:28.920 --> 00:15:32.800
Well, that is because this was our last Halloween episode.
嗯，那是因为这是我们最后一集万圣节特辑了。

360
00:15:33.180 --> 00:15:33.820
Ever.
永远的最后一集。

361
00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:34.560
Ever.
最后一集。

362
00:15:34.960 --> 00:15:35.300
Aw.
啊。

363
00:15:35.660 --> 00:15:39.440
And we all did interviews about it and how we were feeling about it.
我们都接受了采访，谈了谈对此的感受。

364
00:15:39.620 --> 00:15:39.940
Yeah.
是啊。

365
00:15:39.940 --> 00:15:46.160
And basically, we were all feeling sad that it was our last one, but also grateful that
基本上，我们都很伤心这是最后一集，但也心怀感激，因为

366
00:15:46.160 --> 00:15:48.060
we got to do a full Halloween episode.
我们能完整地拍完一集万圣节特辑。

367
00:15:48.060 --> 00:15:51.080
I remember being excited that we got to be in costume the whole week.
我记得当时很兴奋，因为我们整整一周都能穿戏服。

368
00:15:51.280 --> 00:15:51.400
Yeah.
是啊。

369
00:15:52.560 --> 00:15:55.820
Well, lastly, the high was 89 degrees.
最后，最高气温是89华氏度。

370
00:15:56.300 --> 00:15:56.960
Thank you.
谢谢。

371
00:15:57.140 --> 00:15:58.540
It was in the 80s this week.
这周气温都在80多度。

372
00:15:58.680 --> 00:15:59.340
That's nice.
那挺好的。

373
00:15:59.420 --> 00:16:00.100
It's an improvement.
算是有所好转了。

374
00:16:00.400 --> 00:16:04.100
Well, like we said, this is our Halloween episode and Dwight is gonna enter the office
嗯，就像我们说的，这是我们的万圣节特辑，德怀特会顶着

375
00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:06.520
with a giant pumpkin on his head.
一个巨大的南瓜头走进办公室。

376
00:16:06.860 --> 00:16:07.980
He scares Aaron.
他吓到了亚伦。

377
00:16:08.260 --> 00:16:09.120
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

378
00:16:09.120 --> 00:16:13.480
Every Halloween, I see this picture of Rain with the pumpkin head everywhere.
每个万圣节，我到处都能看到雷恩戴着南瓜头的照片。

379
00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:15.600
It's like on t-shirts, on stickers.
印在T恤上，贴纸上，到处都是。

380
00:16:15.780 --> 00:16:16.220
It's everywhere.
到处都是。

381
00:16:16.420 --> 00:16:17.320
Well, there's a problem.
嗯，有个问题。

382
00:16:17.580 --> 00:16:19.340
He can't get the pumpkin head off.
他摘不下那个南瓜头。

383
00:16:19.460 --> 00:16:19.980
He cannot.
确实摘不下来。

384
00:16:20.380 --> 00:16:22.340
We had a fan question from Olivia H.
我们收到了一位粉丝奥利维亚·H的提问，

385
00:16:22.460 --> 00:16:24.360
in Minneapolis, Minnesota, who said,
她来自明尼苏达州明尼阿波利斯，她说，

386
00:16:24.520 --> 00:16:28.600
The Dwight pumpkin head cold open is my single favorite cold open in the entire series.
德怀特戴南瓜头的开场戏是我整部剧里最喜欢的开场。

387
00:16:28.800 --> 00:16:32.380
I watch it whenever I'm feeling down and it never fails to brighten my day.
每当我心情低落时就会看，它总能让我振作起来。

388
00:16:32.700 --> 00:16:34.060
Please tell me everything.
请告诉我一切细节。

389
00:16:34.060 --> 00:16:35.660
Were there any scenes cut out?
有删减掉的戏份吗？

390
00:16:35.880 --> 00:16:36.940
I must know.
我一定要知道。

391
00:16:36.940 --> 00:16:42.700
And Mia Oh, a middle schooler from Cedar Park, Texas, wanted to know if the pumpkin was real.
还有来自德克萨斯州锡达帕克的初中生米娅·奥，她想知道那个南瓜是不是真的。

392
00:16:42.900 --> 00:16:43.960
We have the answers.
我们有答案。

393
00:16:44.260 --> 00:16:45.620
Mia, I'll tell you this.
米娅，我告诉你吧。

394
00:16:45.620 --> 00:16:49.100
We used a real pumpkin to fit Rain.
我们确实用了一个真南瓜来给雷恩试戴。

395
00:16:49.540 --> 00:16:51.760
We carved out a pumpkin just like that.
我们把南瓜掏空，就是那样做的。

396
00:16:51.760 --> 00:17:03.100
But about a week before the episode, the costumers took that real pumpkin to a molder who made a fiberglass version because we didn't want it to rot or break.
但在拍摄前一周左右，服装师把那个真南瓜拿去给模具师做了一个玻璃纤维版本，因为我们不想让它腐烂或破裂。

397
00:17:03.980 --> 00:17:12.420
And Steve Burgess sent us a very funny photo of Rain with the fiberglass pumpkin on his head trying to read his sides through the eye hole.
史蒂夫·伯吉斯发给我们一张非常有趣的照片，雷恩戴着玻璃纤维南瓜头，正试图通过眼孔看剧本。

398
00:17:13.920 --> 00:17:17.120
So Rain really did walk around with that thing for a while.
所以雷恩确实顶着那玩意儿走来走去了一段时间。

399
00:17:17.360 --> 00:17:19.400
I should say Steve sends us great pictures.
我得说史蒂夫发给我们的照片都很棒。

400
00:17:19.520 --> 00:17:25.740
He also sent me a photo I had never seen of myself and the senator as Nancy and Ronald Reagan.
他还发给我一张我从未见过的照片，是我和参议员扮成南希·里根和罗纳德·里根的样子。

401
00:17:26.200 --> 00:17:27.560
I'll put all of these in stories.
我会把这些都发到快拍里。

402
00:17:27.740 --> 00:17:29.900
Claire sent us a ton of great pictures, too.
克莱尔也给我们发了好多很棒的照片。

403
00:17:30.100 --> 00:17:32.740
We're going to have a lot of pictures for Instagram this week.
这周我们会有很多照片可以发到Instagram上。

404
00:17:32.740 --> 00:17:34.320
Yes, a lot of behind-the-scenes photos.
没错，有很多幕后花絮照。

405
00:17:34.800 --> 00:17:41.300
And Olivia, to answer your question, there were several more scenes with Dwight with this pumpkin on his head.
还有奥利维亚，回答你的问题，德怀特头上套着南瓜的戏份其实还有好几场。

406
00:17:41.880 --> 00:17:50.340
Ultimately, what happens in deleted scenes is Dwight is backing out of the parking lot with the big pumpkin head, and his car hits the row of hedges.
最终，在删减片段里发生的事是，德怀特顶着那个大南瓜头从停车场倒车出来，结果车撞上了一排树篱。

407
00:17:50.520 --> 00:17:57.820
His head kind of slams into the side of the car's interior, and the pumpkin starts to break in half, and he's able to free himself.
他的头撞到了车内侧，南瓜开始裂成两半，他才得以脱身。

408
00:17:58.060 --> 00:17:59.800
Oh, so we got to see him freed.
哦，所以我们能看到他脱困的过程。

409
00:17:59.800 --> 00:18:04.860
Yes, and he throws the pumpkin pieces out the window and is like, ha-ha, and he drives off.
是的，他把南瓜碎片扔出窗外，还哈哈大笑，然后开车走了。

410
00:18:05.120 --> 00:18:09.200
And Claire, our director, shared with us that this scene was actually really difficult to shoot.
我们的导演克莱尔跟我们分享说，这场戏其实拍起来非常困难。

411
00:18:09.400 --> 00:18:18.240
She said that pumpkin head was so big that they had to pull the driver's seat out of the car so Rain could physically get in the car,
她说那个南瓜头太大了，他们不得不把驾驶座拆掉，雷恩才能钻进车里，

412
00:18:18.260 --> 00:18:20.720
and they could film him with the pumpkin head getting in the car.
这样他们才能拍到他顶着南瓜头钻进车的镜头。

413
00:18:20.880 --> 00:18:21.060
Yeah.
是啊。

414
00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:26.100
And then after all that trouble, they never used any of the footage of him getting in the car.
结果费了这么大劲，他们最后根本没用那些他钻进车的镜头。

415
00:18:26.100 --> 00:18:31.100
Claire also shared that when they were shooting Rain's talking head with the pumpkin head on,
克莱尔还分享说，当他们拍摄雷恩戴着南瓜头的采访镜头时，

416
00:18:31.280 --> 00:18:36.900
that at first they thought that they could just put any words in his mouth because the pumpkin kind of covered everything.
起初他们以为可以随便配音，因为南瓜把脸都遮住了。

417
00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:42.540
But then they realized when they got in editing that you could still see his mouth kind of moving.
但后来剪辑时他们发现，还是能看到他的嘴在动。

418
00:18:42.840 --> 00:18:46.580
And she said if you look close enough, it's a little bit out of sync.
她说如果你仔细看，会发现有点对不上口型。

419
00:18:46.840 --> 00:18:52.240
When he says the pumpkin should rot off my head in a month or two, it doesn't totally match.
当他说“南瓜应该会在一两个月内从我头上烂掉”时，口型完全对不上。

420
00:18:52.240 --> 00:18:52.960
Exactly.
确实。

421
00:18:53.480 --> 00:18:59.060
I will tell you that I looked up people wearing pumpkin heads at Halloween.
我得告诉你，我特意去查了万圣节戴南瓜头的人。

422
00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:00.280
Like, are people doing this?
就是说，真的有人这么做吗？

423
00:19:00.360 --> 00:19:02.420
I did find some people did this.
我还真发现有人这么干。

424
00:19:02.540 --> 00:19:04.000
They carved out a pumpkin like Dwight.
他们像德怀特一样把南瓜掏空。

425
00:19:04.380 --> 00:19:04.620
Really?
真的吗？

426
00:19:04.740 --> 00:19:07.540
Yes, and they took photos of themselves, the TikTokers.
是的，那些TikTok博主还给自己拍了照。

427
00:19:08.220 --> 00:19:09.620
The talkers did it?
博主们也这么干？

428
00:19:09.660 --> 00:19:10.740
The talkers did it.
博主们也这么干。

429
00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:17.820
And then I was curious if you could buy a pumpkin head like the one Dwight wore and make your own Halloween costume.
然后我很好奇，能不能买到像德怀特戴的那种南瓜头来做万圣节服装。

430
00:19:17.820 --> 00:19:21.760
I did find a plushy version on Amazon.
我在亚马逊上确实找到了一个毛绒版的。

431
00:19:22.200 --> 00:19:24.240
I'm surprised this isn't a costume.
我很惊讶这居然不是现成的服装。

432
00:19:24.680 --> 00:19:24.960
Yeah.
是啊。

433
00:19:25.280 --> 00:19:28.060
Well, we got an interesting fan question from Ayla R.
好吧，我们收到一个来自挪威的艾拉·R的有趣粉丝提问，

434
00:19:28.180 --> 00:19:31.260
in Norway, Angela, that I thought maybe we could discuss.
安吉拉，我觉得我们可以讨论一下。

435
00:19:31.660 --> 00:19:31.760
Okay.
好啊。

436
00:19:32.140 --> 00:19:39.640
Ayla notes that in order to make his costume, Dwight had to carve out the bottom of the pumpkin.
艾拉指出，为了做他的服装，德怀特必须把南瓜底部掏空。

437
00:19:39.900 --> 00:19:42.180
He had to put the hole in the bottom of the pumpkin.
他必须在南瓜底部开个洞。

438
00:19:42.400 --> 00:19:43.360
Pull all the stuff out.
把里面的东西都掏出来。

439
00:19:43.360 --> 00:19:50.720
Yes, and Ayla said that this reminded her of the big debate over the best way to carve a pumpkin.
没错，艾拉说这让她想起了关于雕刻南瓜的最佳方式的激烈争论。

440
00:19:51.120 --> 00:19:59.420
Do you cut a hole in the top and scoop it out from the top, or do you put a hole in the bottom and scoop it out from the bottom?
你是从顶部开洞掏空，还是从底部开洞掏空？

441
00:19:59.580 --> 00:20:01.900
Ayla wanted to know, how do we do our pumpkins?
艾拉想知道，我们是怎么处理南瓜的？

442
00:20:02.420 --> 00:20:05.340
Ayla, I did not know there was a great pumpkin debate.
艾拉，我以前都不知道还有关于南瓜的“大争论”。

443
00:20:05.860 --> 00:20:06.220
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

444
00:20:06.760 --> 00:20:10.280
I always do the top and then make a little hat.
我总是从顶部切开，然后做一个小盖子。

