00:26:38.820 --> 00:26:39.640
And they'd be like, oh, my God.
他们就会说，天哪。

607
00:26:40.360 --> 00:26:42.020
It just freaked everyone out.
这把所有人都吓坏了。

608
00:26:42.240 --> 00:26:44.940
And one day for lunch, my daughter came to set.
有一天午餐时，我女儿来片场了。

609
00:26:45.080 --> 00:26:46.700
And she was like, no, no, no, no, mama.
她当时说，不，不，不，不，妈妈。

610
00:26:46.860 --> 00:26:47.640
No, no, mama.
不，不，妈妈。

611
00:26:47.820 --> 00:26:49.820
She was like, get rid of that wig.
她说，把那顶假发摘掉。

612
00:26:49.820 --> 00:26:51.700
But I couldn't take it off all day.
但我一整天都摘不下来。

613
00:26:52.140 --> 00:26:52.260
Yeah.
是啊。

614
00:26:52.360 --> 00:26:54.140
I had to wear wigs for Walk Hard.
拍《永不止步》时我也得戴假发。

615
00:26:54.140 --> 00:26:55.520
And it was the same thing.
情况也是一样。

616
00:26:55.660 --> 00:26:59.220
They do the little pin curls of your hair to your head.
他们会把你的头发卷成小卷贴在头上。

617
00:26:59.300 --> 00:27:00.240
They put on this bald cap.
戴上秃头套。

618
00:27:00.380 --> 00:27:01.560
And then they stick it on you.
然后把假发粘在你头上。

619
00:27:01.620 --> 00:27:03.360
And it takes a long time.
这很花时间。

620
00:27:03.580 --> 00:27:03.780
Yeah.
是啊。

621
00:27:03.780 --> 00:27:04.880
And then you're in it.
然后你就得一直戴着它。

622
00:27:05.000 --> 00:27:05.660
You're in it.
一直戴着。

623
00:27:05.720 --> 00:27:06.260
You're in it.
一直戴着。

624
00:27:06.440 --> 00:27:09.320
And you're in whatever clothes you were in before you got it on.
而且你还得穿着戴上它之前穿的衣服。

625
00:27:09.480 --> 00:27:09.680
Yeah.
是啊。

626
00:27:10.200 --> 00:27:13.080
And you, Jenna, in particular, this wig really tickled you.
而你，珍娜，尤其是你，这顶假发真的把你逗乐了。

627
00:27:13.220 --> 00:27:14.500
You could barely look at me.
你几乎不敢看我。

628
00:27:14.800 --> 00:27:18.540
I remember I walked up to you just like on a break eating a cheese stick.
我记得有次休息时，我走近你，当时你正在吃奶酪棒。

629
00:27:18.540 --> 00:27:19.700
And you're like, I can't.
你说，我不行了。

630
00:27:19.760 --> 00:27:21.720
I can't look at you in that wig.
我没法看着戴那顶假发的你。

631
00:27:21.800 --> 00:27:22.960
You're eating cheese.
你还在吃奶酪。

632
00:27:24.980 --> 00:27:30.120
Well, Andy's going to go on to explain that these guys are from the Cornell acapella group
安迪接下来会解释说，这些人来自康奈尔大学的无伴奏合唱团

633
00:27:30.120 --> 00:27:31.020
Here Comes Trouble.
“麻烦来了”。

634
00:27:31.160 --> 00:27:34.340
And they will be performing for all of us at the Halloween party today.
他们今天会在万圣节派对上为我们所有人表演。

635
00:27:35.060 --> 00:27:38.080
Meredith would like to know a little bit more about the sleeping arrangements.
梅雷迪思想多了解一下住宿安排。

636
00:27:38.120 --> 00:27:38.660
Oh, Meredith.
噢，梅雷迪思。

637
00:27:39.100 --> 00:27:40.700
For all these guys while they're in town.
这些人来城里期间的住宿。

638
00:27:41.100 --> 00:27:42.660
Stanley just says he's not interested.
斯坦利直接说他没兴趣。

639
00:27:43.020 --> 00:27:43.200
No.
不。

640
00:27:43.340 --> 00:27:44.600
I'm not interested in sitting through that.
我没兴趣坐在那儿听那个。

641
00:27:44.600 --> 00:27:44.860
He doesn't care.
他根本不在乎。

642
00:27:45.980 --> 00:27:48.960
Andy's going to have a talking head where he says, you know what?
安迪会有一个单独采访，他说，你知道吗？

643
00:27:48.960 --> 00:27:55.140
He just realized, he just realized they might call him up to sing his signature song, Faith.
他刚意识到，他刚意识到他们可能会叫他上去唱他的招牌歌曲《Faith》。

644
00:27:55.340 --> 00:27:55.980
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

645
00:27:55.980 --> 00:28:00.400
I'm dressed as George Michael and they might call me up to sing Faith.
我打扮成乔治·迈克尔的样子，他们可能会叫我上去唱《Faith》。

646
00:28:00.400 --> 00:28:00.980
Come on.
拜托。

647
00:28:01.020 --> 00:28:01.800
He's not prepared.
他还没准备好。

648
00:28:02.020 --> 00:28:03.000
Oh, he's not prepared at all.
噢，他一点准备都没有。

649
00:28:03.060 --> 00:28:04.260
He hasn't even really thought that through.
他甚至都没怎么考虑过这件事。

650
00:28:04.940 --> 00:28:09.560
Jim is now going to leave for his big meeting and he just double checks with Pam.
吉姆现在要出发去参加他的重要会议了，他跟帕姆再次确认了一下。

651
00:28:09.560 --> 00:28:10.980
You still good that I'm going to invest?
你还觉得我应该去投资吗？

652
00:28:11.660 --> 00:28:12.700
And she's like, yeah.
她说，是的。

653
00:28:13.140 --> 00:28:13.480
Right?
对吧？

654
00:28:13.680 --> 00:28:13.840
Yeah.
没错。

655
00:28:13.840 --> 00:28:14.600
We got to do this.
我们得这么做。

656
00:28:14.800 --> 00:28:15.640
We're going to do it.
我们一定要做。

657
00:28:15.700 --> 00:28:16.240
Let's do it.
干吧。

658
00:28:16.240 --> 00:28:20.200
So it's important for me to share with everyone that this scene was scripted a little differently
所以我想告诉大家，这一幕的剧本其实和最终播出的版本有点不同，

659
00:28:20.200 --> 00:28:22.500
than how it ended up in the episode.
这一点很重要。

660
00:28:22.740 --> 00:28:26.140
And this is going to affect the storyline as we go on.
而且这会影响后续的剧情发展。

661
00:28:26.480 --> 00:28:29.100
The scene was originally scripted like this.
这一幕原本的剧本是这样的：

662
00:28:29.660 --> 00:28:32.380
Pam says, it's almost noon.
帕姆说，快中午了。

663
00:28:32.640 --> 00:28:34.580
Don't you need to go blow a hole in our savings?
你不需要去把我们的积蓄挥霍掉吗？

664
00:28:35.100 --> 00:28:37.120
There's a little of her angry sarcasm.
她带了点愤怒的讽刺。

665
00:28:38.400 --> 00:28:40.140
And Jim says, that's right.
吉姆说，没错。

666
00:28:40.140 --> 00:28:41.760
I knew I was forgetting to do something.
我差点忘了这事。

667
00:28:41.760 --> 00:28:47.580
And then he pauses and he said, was that an all in good fun thing or?
然后他停顿了一下，说，你那是开玩笑的，还是认真的？

668
00:28:47.900 --> 00:28:49.100
And Pam says, yes.
帕姆说，是认真的。

669
00:28:49.580 --> 00:28:54.220
And then Jim says, you sure you're cool with putting in $5,000?
然后吉姆说，你确定你愿意投入五千美元？

670
00:28:54.900 --> 00:28:55.060
Yeah.
是的。

671
00:28:55.420 --> 00:28:56.700
And she says, yeah.
她说，是的。

672
00:28:56.860 --> 00:28:59.460
I mean, if we're going to do this thing, we should do it, right?
我是说，既然我们要干，就得干到底，对吧？

673
00:28:59.700 --> 00:29:01.500
And Jim says, you're the beSt.
吉姆说，你真是太棒了。

674
00:29:01.520 --> 00:29:03.740
And Pam says, seriously, I am.
帕姆说，说真的，我确实很棒。

675
00:29:03.860 --> 00:29:04.360
It's crazy.
太疯狂了。

676
00:29:04.920 --> 00:29:13.020
So I just want to say that in this story, Pam said that Jim could invest $5,000.
所以我只想说，在这个故事里，帕姆是同意吉姆投资五千美元的。

677
00:29:13.920 --> 00:29:15.120
Well, it's what they agreed on.
嗯，这是他们商量好的。

678
00:29:15.280 --> 00:29:15.740
Yes.
没错。

679
00:29:15.920 --> 00:29:16.920
They had a conversation.
他们确实谈过。

680
00:29:17.280 --> 00:29:25.880
So later in the episode, when he puts in $10,000, that is, again, not what they agreed on when they talked at home.
所以后来在剧集中，当他投入一万美元时，那确实不是他们在家里商量好的金额。

681
00:29:25.920 --> 00:29:28.120
And that is why Pam is going to get so mad.
这就是为什么帕姆会那么生气。

682
00:29:28.120 --> 00:29:32.240
And I think it's kind of a bummer that that little tidbit got cut out.
我觉得这段小插曲被删掉挺可惜的。

683
00:29:32.460 --> 00:29:32.600
Right.
确实。

684
00:29:33.060 --> 00:29:38.660
Because otherwise, it just seems like Pam is angry that Jim did something that they agreed to.
因为如果不交代这些，看起来就像是吉姆明明做了他们商量好的事，帕姆却无理取闹。

685
00:29:38.900 --> 00:29:39.040
Right.
没错。

686
00:29:39.060 --> 00:29:42.720
But the truth is, the way it was originally written, he didn't.
但事实是，按照最初的剧本，他并没有按约定行事。

687
00:29:43.060 --> 00:29:43.220
Right.
对。

688
00:29:43.900 --> 00:29:48.240
As Jim leaves, Dwight is going to hold up a little box of nerds candy.
吉姆离开时，德怀特会举起一小盒“书呆子”糖果。

689
00:29:48.240 --> 00:29:51.140
And he's like, look, I'm eating a gym.
他说，看，我在吃吉姆。

690
00:29:51.420 --> 00:29:51.980
Get it?
懂了吗？

691
00:29:52.060 --> 00:29:52.780
Because it's a nerd.
因为那是书呆子（Nerd）。

692
00:29:52.980 --> 00:29:53.300
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

693
00:29:53.520 --> 00:29:55.760
Aaron finds this hilarious.
艾琳觉得这太搞笑了。

694
00:29:56.300 --> 00:29:56.620
Yes.
是的。

695
00:29:56.620 --> 00:29:58.800
We had a fan question from Nick R.
我们收到了一位来自伊利诺伊州皮奥里亚的粉丝尼克·R的提问，他说，

696
00:29:58.960 --> 00:30:00.560
in Peoria, Illinois, who said,
“艾琳在这一幕中响亮的笑声似乎让她和德怀特都做出了真实的反应。

697
00:30:01.080 --> 00:30:06.780
Aaron's loud laugh in this scene seemed to generate a genuine reaction for both her and Dwight.
这是剧本写的，还是意外收获的惊喜？

698
00:30:06.980 --> 00:30:10.320
Was it scripted or left in as a happy little accident?
不管怎样，都太棒了。”

699
00:30:10.640 --> 00:30:11.840
Either way, it's so great.
尼克，这是剧本写的。

700
00:30:12.060 --> 00:30:13.540
Nick, it was scripted.
尼克，这是剧本写的。

701
00:30:13.740 --> 00:30:15.420
It says, Dwight says Jim is a nerd.
上面写着，德怀特说吉姆是个书呆子。

702
00:30:15.580 --> 00:30:16.780
This is a box of geMs.
这是一盒宝石。

703
00:30:17.000 --> 00:30:18.040
And Aaron laughs.
然后艾琳笑了。

704
00:30:18.160 --> 00:30:21.920
And then it says in all caps, really loud and covers her mouth.
接着上面用大写字母写着，声音很大，还捂住了她的嘴。

705
00:30:22.660 --> 00:30:25.340
And then it says, Aaron keeps laughing, keeps laughing,
然后上面写着，艾琳一直在笑，一直在笑，

706
00:30:25.340 --> 00:30:27.540
until she has to run towards the bathroom.
直到她不得不跑向洗手间。

707
00:30:27.840 --> 00:30:29.800
Well, we also had a fan question from Barb B.
嗯，我们还收到了一位来自威斯康星州的芭布·B的粉丝提问，

708
00:30:29.880 --> 00:30:31.380
in Wisconsin, who said,
她说，

709
00:30:31.480 --> 00:30:33.980
when Dwight makes Aaron laugh so hard, she has to pee.
当德怀特把艾琳逗得大笑，以至于她不得不去尿尿时。

710
00:30:34.180 --> 00:30:40.500
Was this a nod to the Work Bus episode when Ellie as Aaron actually peed from laughing so hard?
这是在向《工作巴士》那一集致敬吗？当时艾莉饰演的艾琳真的因为笑得太厉害而尿裤子了？

711
00:30:40.720 --> 00:30:41.780
I wondered that.
我也想过这个问题。

712
00:30:41.900 --> 00:30:42.820
I did too.
我也是。

713
00:30:42.820 --> 00:30:44.840
I mean, it had literally just happened.
我的意思是，这确实刚刚发生过。

714
00:30:45.120 --> 00:30:47.640
This episode comes right after Work Bus.
这一集就在《工作巴士》之后。

715
00:30:47.720 --> 00:30:47.860
Yes.
是的。

716
00:30:48.100 --> 00:30:50.060
And we all had this collective story.
我们都有这段共同的记忆。

717
00:30:50.440 --> 00:30:52.140
I feel like it must have.
我觉得一定是这样。

718
00:30:52.240 --> 00:30:52.620
I know.
我知道。

719
00:30:53.100 --> 00:30:55.620
Well, Ellie was a good sport about all of it.
嗯，艾莉对这一切表现得很大度。

720
00:30:55.740 --> 00:30:57.840
So no doubt she was like fine with it.
所以毫无疑问，她对此没意见。

721
00:30:58.140 --> 00:31:00.260
Well, Dwight drops a bunch of gems on the ground.
德怀特把一堆宝石掉在了地上。

722
00:31:00.260 --> 00:31:01.300
He's picking them up.
他正在捡它们。

723
00:31:01.460 --> 00:31:04.700
And while doing so, he finds a little yellow pill.
在捡的时候，他发现了一颗黄色的小药丸。

724
00:31:05.360 --> 00:31:05.720
Yeah.
是的。

725
00:31:05.720 --> 00:31:09.620
He has a talking head where he says, it's Dumatril.
他有一个单人采访，他说，这是杜马特里尔。

726
00:31:10.080 --> 00:31:15.500
It treats anxiety symptoms such as panic attacks, excessive worrying, and fear.
它用于治疗焦虑症状，如恐慌发作、过度担忧和恐惧。

727
00:31:16.460 --> 00:31:18.560
Translation, there's a madman in our midSt.
翻译一下就是，我们中间出了个疯子。

728
00:31:19.080 --> 00:31:21.700
This is now going to be his storyline for the rest of the episode.
这现在成了他这一集剩余部分的故事线。

729
00:31:21.700 --> 00:31:25.120
He has got to find out whose pill this is.
他必须找出这颗药丸是谁的。

730
00:31:25.240 --> 00:31:26.720
He's going to mom detective it.
他要像个妈妈侦探一样去调查。

731
00:31:26.880 --> 00:31:27.120
Yes.
是的。

732
00:31:27.560 --> 00:31:29.260
FYI, Dumatril does not exiSt.
顺便说一下，杜马特里尔并不存在。

733
00:31:29.460 --> 00:31:30.260
It's made up.
它是虚构的。

734
00:31:30.260 --> 00:31:30.900
It's a made up.
它是编出来的。

735
00:31:31.980 --> 00:31:33.280
We now see Nellie.
我们现在看到了奈莉。

736
00:31:33.440 --> 00:31:35.220
She is dressed as Sexy Toby.
她打扮成了性感托比。

737
00:31:36.120 --> 00:31:39.680
And she shares in a talking head that the anxiety pill is hers.
她在单人采访中承认那颗抗焦虑药是她的。

738
00:31:40.020 --> 00:31:44.120
She's not ashamed of it, but she doesn't love the idea of Dwight having that information
她并不为此感到羞耻，但她不喜欢德怀特掌握她这个信息，

739
00:31:44.120 --> 00:31:47.440
about her since he once yelled at Phyllis for sneezing wrong.
因为他曾经因为菲利斯打喷嚏的方式不对而对她大吼大叫。

740
00:31:47.920 --> 00:31:53.480
Nellie agrees with Dwight that, you know, the person who owns this pill needs to be apprehended.
奈莉同意德怀特的观点，你知道的，拥有这颗药丸的人需要被逮捕。

741
00:31:53.620 --> 00:31:56.540
So Dwight is going to go get his apprehension kit.
所以德怀特要去拿他的逮捕工具包。

742
00:31:56.740 --> 00:31:57.000
Yeah.
是的。

743
00:31:57.000 --> 00:32:01.220
And now he's got a partner to help solve this mystery.
现在他有了一个帮手来解开这个谜团。

744
00:32:01.700 --> 00:32:07.580
Lady, do we need an apprehension kit for mom detectives in case we have to apprehend someone?
女士，我们需要为妈妈侦探准备一个逮捕工具包，以防我们需要逮捕某人吗？

745
00:32:07.580 --> 00:32:11.760
Or if we have to go on a stakeout, like I feel like it would all be in the same kit.
或者如果我们必须去蹲点，我觉得这些东西应该都在同一个工具包里。

746
00:32:11.900 --> 00:32:13.260
We need snacks and water.
我们需要零食和水。

747
00:32:13.640 --> 00:32:14.080
Flashlight?
手电筒？

748
00:32:14.720 --> 00:32:15.400
Flashlight's good.
手电筒不错。

749
00:32:15.640 --> 00:32:19.420
I think we should have the ones that go on our heads so that we can be hands-free.
我觉得我们应该准备那种戴在头上的，这样我们可以腾出双手。

750
00:32:19.540 --> 00:32:19.960
Oh, yes, yes.
哦，对，没错。

751
00:32:20.180 --> 00:32:20.620
Headlamp.
头灯。

752
00:32:20.920 --> 00:32:21.360
Headlamp.
头灯。

753
00:32:21.980 --> 00:32:22.420
Snacks.
零食。

754
00:32:22.680 --> 00:32:23.480
A blanket.
一条毯子。

755
00:32:23.500 --> 00:32:24.300
I'll be cold.
我会冷的。

756
00:32:25.000 --> 00:32:25.300
Yeah.
没错。

757
00:32:25.940 --> 00:32:26.380
Megaphone?
扩音器？

758
00:32:27.340 --> 00:32:27.860
Smart.
聪明。

759
00:32:28.520 --> 00:32:29.040
Megaphone.
扩音器。

760
00:32:29.240 --> 00:32:29.720
Yes.
好的。

761
00:32:30.420 --> 00:32:30.820
Yeah.
没错。

762
00:32:31.180 --> 00:32:33.940
Rather than sneak up, let's go in hot.
与其潜入，不如大张旗鼓地进去。

763
00:32:34.120 --> 00:32:35.680
Be like, we see you.
就像是说，我们看到你了。

764
00:32:36.420 --> 00:32:36.940
Yeah.
没错。

765
00:32:37.180 --> 00:32:39.700
We should get one of those things that makes things bigger.
我们应该弄个能把东西放大的玩意儿。

766
00:32:39.940 --> 00:32:41.000
A magnifying glass?
放大镜？

767
00:32:41.180 --> 00:32:41.520
Yes.
对。

768
00:32:43.920 --> 00:32:44.440
Yes.
没错。

769
00:32:44.680 --> 00:32:47.020
In case we have to look at tiny evidence.
