布朗尼蛋糕和姜饼放在同一个盘子里？

1092
00:45:37.490 --> 00:45:38.770
Where was the logic there?
逻辑在哪里？

1093
00:45:38.950 --> 00:45:40.530
I mean, what was going through your mind?
我是说，你当时脑子里在想什么？

1094
00:45:40.890 --> 00:45:44.110
I just thought it was a party and people wouldn't think too much about it.
我只是觉得这就是个派对，大家不会太在意这些。

1095
00:45:44.810 --> 00:45:45.250
Ridiculous.
荒谬。

1096
00:45:45.870 --> 00:45:49.370
You know, this is what happens when I give you a long leash, but you are not getting within
你知道，这就是我给你太多自由的结果，但圣诞派对的时候，

1097
00:45:49.370 --> 00:45:51.450
a mile of the snacks table for the Christmas party.
你离零食桌一英里以内都不准靠近。

1098
00:45:51.650 --> 00:45:52.470
Yeah, I understand.
好的，我明白了。

1099
00:45:52.470 --> 00:45:53.930
I feel bad about this.
我对此感到很抱歉。

1100
00:45:54.090 --> 00:45:54.390
Good.
很好。

1101
00:45:55.730 --> 00:45:58.370
Maybe the cupcakes with the ginger snaps?
也许配上姜汁饼干怎么样？

1102
00:45:58.490 --> 00:46:00.150
No, nothing should be with the ginger snaps.
不，什么都不该配姜汁饼干。

1103
00:46:00.290 --> 00:46:02.030
Ginger snaps are off-putting to some people.
有些人觉得姜汁饼干很倒胃口。

1104
00:46:02.250 --> 00:46:02.910
What's your favorite?
你最喜欢什么？

1105
00:46:03.530 --> 00:46:06.330
Maybe you shouldn't be in charge of arranging the snacks.
也许你不该负责安排零食。

1106
00:46:07.730 --> 00:46:08.850
Don't go there, sweetie.
别那样，亲爱的。

1107
00:46:09.130 --> 00:46:09.850
Don't you go there.
你别那样。

1108
00:46:10.110 --> 00:46:11.090
Do your job.
做好你的工作。

1109
00:46:13.360 --> 00:46:15.460
Phyllis goes, don't you go there, sweetie.
菲利斯说，别那样，亲爱的。

1110
00:46:15.640 --> 00:46:18.720
And then under her breath, Angela says, do your job.
然后安吉拉小声嘀咕了一句，做好你的工作。

1111
00:46:19.920 --> 00:46:22.340
It is so layered with tension.
这其中充满了张力。

1112
00:46:22.900 --> 00:46:24.220
And you know what?
而且你知道吗？

1113
00:46:24.240 --> 00:46:27.060
If you get a sweetie out of Phyllis, get ready.
如果你从菲利斯那儿听到“亲爱的”，就做好准备吧。

1114
00:46:27.200 --> 00:46:27.420
Yeah.
是啊。

1115
00:46:27.540 --> 00:46:28.580
She's about to throw down.
她要发火了。

1116
00:46:29.400 --> 00:46:33.900
Erin is trying to make Andy feel better about the group.
艾琳正试图让安迪对这个团队感觉好一点。

1117
00:46:33.900 --> 00:46:37.680
Not really maybe being super excited about his Boner Champ story.
可能并不是对他那个“硬汉冠军”的故事特别兴奋。

1118
00:46:38.000 --> 00:46:38.340
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1119
00:46:38.760 --> 00:46:41.040
Erin is like, what is wrong with these turkeys?
艾琳心想，这些蠢货到底怎么回事？

1120
00:46:41.400 --> 00:46:45.820
Yeah, she marches into the break room and says, hey, you have to sing Faith.
是啊，她走进休息室说，嘿，你们必须唱《Faith》。

1121
00:46:46.120 --> 00:46:46.740
Learn it.
去学一下。

1122
00:46:47.160 --> 00:46:47.500
Yeah.
是啊。

1123
00:46:47.640 --> 00:46:48.620
Just do it.
直接唱就行。

1124
00:46:49.080 --> 00:46:50.400
And the guy's like, but, but.
那家伙说，但是，但是。

1125
00:46:50.500 --> 00:46:52.160
And she goes, butts are for pooping.
然后她说，屁股是用来拉屎的。

1126
00:46:52.400 --> 00:46:53.540
Make it work.
把它搞定。

1127
00:46:54.220 --> 00:46:55.620
And make it a surprise.
而且要给个惊喜。

1128
00:46:56.520 --> 00:46:59.260
Meanwhile, Dwight and Nellie are camped out in the kitchen.
与此同时，德怀特和奈莉在厨房里蹲守。

1129
00:46:59.260 --> 00:47:01.260
The pill is on a plate on the counter.
药片放在柜台上的盘子里。

1130
00:47:01.460 --> 00:47:03.420
And they're doing a steak out, lady.
他们正在进行一场“牛排蹲守”，女士。

1131
00:47:03.420 --> 00:47:04.140
I know.
我知道。

1132
00:47:04.400 --> 00:47:07.040
Toby is going to enter the steak out.
托比打算加入这场蹲守。

1133
00:47:07.300 --> 00:47:10.120
And he sees Nellie in her costume.
他看到了穿着戏服的奈莉。

1134
00:47:10.120 --> 00:47:12.300
And he recognizes himself.
他认出了那是他自己。

1135
00:47:12.540 --> 00:47:14.140
He seems very transfixed.
他看起来非常出神。

1136
00:47:14.340 --> 00:47:17.700
I was curious what the shooting draft had to say about this moment.
我很好奇拍摄剧本里是怎么描述这一刻的。

1137
00:47:17.700 --> 00:47:18.820
So I looked it up.
所以我查了一下。

1138
00:47:18.960 --> 00:47:20.020
What does it say?
上面怎么说？

1139
00:47:20.220 --> 00:47:22.680
Per the shooting draft, it says,
根据拍摄剧本，上面写着，

1140
00:47:23.460 --> 00:47:24.240
Toby enters.
托比进来了。

1141
00:47:24.940 --> 00:47:26.320
Nellie nods at him.
奈莉向他点头。

1142
00:47:26.920 --> 00:47:31.880
Toby looks at her with embarrassment, then anger, then luSt.
托比看着她，先是尴尬，然后是愤怒，接着是欲望。

1143
00:47:31.880 --> 00:47:36.540
He briefly moves towards her as if to kiss her, then hurries out.
他短暂地向她靠近，仿佛要亲吻她，然后匆忙离开。

1144
00:47:38.470 --> 00:47:40.430
It's a lot happening in that moment.
那一刻发生了很多事。

1145
00:47:41.070 --> 00:47:41.390
Yeah.
是啊。

1146
00:47:41.670 --> 00:47:46.330
A lot of, I guess, self-loathing and then self-love from Toby.
我想托比当时充满了自我厌恶，然后又是自我爱慕。

1147
00:47:46.330 --> 00:47:47.110
Yeah.
是啊。

1148
00:47:48.410 --> 00:47:49.770
I thought it was weird.
我觉得那很奇怪。

1149
00:47:50.170 --> 00:47:50.830
I know.
我知道。

1150
00:47:50.910 --> 00:47:51.430
I did, too.
我也这么觉得。

1151
00:47:51.710 --> 00:47:52.630
I didn't get it.
我没听懂。

1152
00:47:52.690 --> 00:47:53.510
I didn't get it.
我没听懂。

1153
00:47:53.830 --> 00:47:56.230
Guess who's going to come in and try to claim that pill?
猜猜谁会进来试图认领那颗药丸？

1154
00:47:56.830 --> 00:47:57.310
Meredith.
梅雷迪思。

1155
00:47:57.770 --> 00:47:59.370
She sees it as a free upper.
她觉得那是免费的兴奋剂。

1156
00:48:00.130 --> 00:48:02.070
And Dwight is going to net her.
德怀特会用网兜住她。

1157
00:48:02.230 --> 00:48:04.430
He gets out a giant net.
他拿出了一个巨大的网兜。

1158
00:48:04.430 --> 00:48:07.450
Is this something we need for our steak out bag?
这是我们蹲点包里需要的东西吗？

1159
00:48:07.570 --> 00:48:08.190
I guess so.
我想是吧。

1160
00:48:08.190 --> 00:48:11.150
What could you imagine if we netted the guy who's...
你能想象如果我们网住了那个……的人会怎样吗？

1161
00:48:11.150 --> 00:48:12.130
Or a raccoon.
或者是一只浣熊。

1162
00:48:12.590 --> 00:48:15.350
You think a raccoon is putting the bottles in the bushes?
你觉得是浣熊把瓶子放进灌木丛里的？

1163
00:48:15.450 --> 00:48:18.750
No, but if we go digging in the bushes, we're going to find a varmint.
不，但如果我们去灌木丛里翻找，肯定会发现什么害兽。

1164
00:48:19.530 --> 00:48:20.330
A varmint.
害兽。

1165
00:48:20.450 --> 00:48:21.570
That's what my mom says.
我妈就是这么说的。

1166
00:48:22.690 --> 00:48:24.450
She'll be like, there's varmints out there.
她会说，外面有害兽。

1167
00:48:25.410 --> 00:48:26.670
It is a thick bush.
这灌木丛真茂密。

1168
00:48:27.090 --> 00:48:27.790
Oh, Lord.
天哪。

1169
00:48:27.970 --> 00:48:29.570
There are so many in this episode.
这一集里有太多这种梗了。

1170
00:48:29.570 --> 00:48:30.370
I can't even.
我简直无语了。

1171
00:48:30.490 --> 00:48:31.630
That's what she said, all of them.
那可是她说的，全都是。

1172
00:48:31.790 --> 00:48:31.950
Wow.
哇。

1173
00:48:32.510 --> 00:48:36.110
Kate has one of her famous lines in this episode where she says to Dwight,
凯特在这一集里有一句名台词，她对德怀特说，

1174
00:48:36.110 --> 00:48:37.830
stop bagging my head.
别再往我头上套袋子了。

1175
00:48:38.230 --> 00:48:38.670
Yes.
没错。

1176
00:48:39.010 --> 00:48:41.070
This is the second time he's bagged her.
这是他第二次往她头上套袋子了。

1177
00:48:41.250 --> 00:48:45.250
He had to bag her when she had the bat on her head, and now he's bagging her again.
上次她头上顶着蝙蝠时他套过一次，现在他又套了一次。

1178
00:48:45.510 --> 00:48:46.690
Listen to you, lady.
听听你说的，女士。

1179
00:48:46.930 --> 00:48:47.230
Listen.
听着。

1180
00:48:47.330 --> 00:48:48.170
I know what you're doing.
我知道你在干什么。

1181
00:48:48.370 --> 00:48:49.350
I'm not doing anything.
我什么都没干。

1182
00:48:49.490 --> 00:48:51.610
It's a callback to a previous episode.
这是对之前某一集的呼应。

1183
00:48:51.830 --> 00:48:52.930
Previous episode.
之前那一集。

1184
00:48:53.130 --> 00:48:53.570
Yes.
对。

1185
00:48:53.870 --> 00:48:57.830
I think it's time for a get to know your cast and crew, thanks to the call sheets.
我觉得是时候通过通告单来了解一下我们的演职人员了。

1186
00:48:57.850 --> 00:48:59.230
Who are we going to learn about today?
今天我们要了解谁呢？

1187
00:48:59.470 --> 00:49:00.390
Nick Carbone.
尼克·卡博内。

1188
00:49:00.810 --> 00:49:05.050
Hey, Nick Carbone, my favorite boom operator of all boom operators.
嘿，尼克·卡博内，我最喜欢的收音师，没有之一。

1189
00:49:05.050 --> 00:49:05.810
That's right.
没错。

1190
00:49:06.110 --> 00:49:10.170
It says, Nick loves music, exclamation point.
上面写着，尼克热爱音乐，感叹号。

1191
00:49:10.470 --> 00:49:12.850
In parentheses, like you didn't know that.
括号里写着，好像你不知道似的。

1192
00:49:13.310 --> 00:49:18.130
His love of music came from his father, who took him to a Janus Joplin concert when he was
他对音乐的热爱源于他的父亲，他父亲在他八岁时带他去看了贾尼斯·乔普林的演唱会。

1193
00:49:18.130 --> 00:49:18.990
eight years old.
八岁。

1194
00:49:19.250 --> 00:49:23.350
The house that he grew up in is next door to where Ben currently lives.
他从小长大的房子就在本现在住的房子的隔壁。

1195
00:49:23.590 --> 00:49:24.830
Ben, our sound designer.
本，我们的音效设计师。

1196
00:49:25.350 --> 00:49:26.570
This is how they met.
这就是他们相识的过程。

1197
00:49:26.810 --> 00:49:31.730
One of his first shows was the classic Golden Girls, and that's where he met Kent Zabornak.
他参与的第一批节目之一是经典剧集《黄金女郎》，他就是在那里认识肯特·扎博纳克的。

1198
00:49:32.170 --> 00:49:32.670
Wow.
哇。

1199
00:49:33.230 --> 00:49:34.070
There you go.
就是这样。

1200
00:49:34.070 --> 00:49:37.210
Well, now we're in the conference room, and everyone is seated.
好了，现在我们到了会议室，大家都坐好了。

1201
00:49:37.410 --> 00:49:39.930
They are ready for this a cappella concert.
他们已经为这场阿卡贝拉音乐会做好准备了。

1202
00:49:40.490 --> 00:49:43.250
We did get a fan catch from Allison H.
我们确实收到了来自肯塔基州路易斯维尔的艾莉森·H的提问，

1203
00:49:43.330 --> 00:49:45.810
in Louisville, Kentucky, who said, did they really
她说，他们真的为了派对把会议室的椅子全搬走了，

1204
00:49:45.810 --> 00:49:51.210
clear out all of the conference room chairs for the party and then move all the food out
然后把食物搬出去，

1205
00:49:51.210 --> 00:49:53.490
and put all the chairs back in for the a cappella concert?
又为了阿卡贝拉音乐会把椅子全搬回来了吗？

1206
00:49:53.870 --> 00:49:58.490
This would really be a great opportunity for the B-roll we never see of people moving the tables
这绝对是拍摄那些我们从未见过的、人们把桌椅搬进搬出会议室的空镜头的绝佳机会。

1207
00:49:58.490 --> 00:50:00.210
and chairs in and out of the conference room.
搬进搬出会议室。

1208
00:50:00.550 --> 00:50:04.230
Allison, you were reading from my personal journal because I wrote,
艾莉森，你简直是在读我的私人日记，因为我写道，

1209
00:50:04.230 --> 00:50:06.010
gonna play a bulls**t card here?
要打出一张“胡扯”牌吗？

1210
00:50:06.150 --> 00:50:07.310
Where's all the table of desserts?
甜点桌去哪了？

1211
00:50:07.550 --> 00:50:08.230
Where'd it all go?
全去哪了？

1212
00:50:08.450 --> 00:50:09.190
Who moved it?
谁搬走的？

1213
00:50:10.570 --> 00:50:13.150
This is when Jim is going to get back from his lunch.
这时吉姆正好午餐回来。

1214
00:50:13.290 --> 00:50:14.750
He's going to have a seat next to Pam.
他会坐在帕姆旁边。

1215
00:50:14.890 --> 00:50:16.470
Pam wants to know how to go, how to go.
帕姆想知道该怎么办，该怎么办。

1216
00:50:16.790 --> 00:50:21.010
He just very quickly is able to say that he pledged the full $10,000.
他非常迅速地说他承诺了全额的一万美元投资。

1217
00:50:21.650 --> 00:50:22.010
Yeah.
是啊。

1218
00:50:22.010 --> 00:50:27.050
You know, he says they said they were good on investing, but, you know, he still went all in.
你知道，他说对方表示投资已经够了，但他还是全投了。

1219
00:50:27.310 --> 00:50:29.830
Pam is having an out-of-body experience.
帕姆当时有一种灵魂出窍的感觉。

1220
00:50:29.830 --> 00:50:30.990
She's like, wait, what?
她心想，等等，什么？

1221
00:50:31.330 --> 00:50:31.530
What?
什么？

1222
00:50:32.670 --> 00:50:33.410
$10,000?
一万美元？

1223
00:50:33.710 --> 00:50:35.870
And they did, like, she's processing all of it.
他们确实……她当时正在消化这一切。

1224
00:50:35.950 --> 00:50:36.170
Yeah.
是啊。

1225
00:50:36.430 --> 00:50:42.990
Right as the a cappella group starts to sing and she's being serenaded and pulled into the circle,
就在阿卡贝拉组合开始演唱，她被歌声包围并拉进圈子时，

1226
00:50:42.990 --> 00:50:44.670
they roll her chair.
他们把她的椅子推走了。

1227
00:50:45.110 --> 00:50:48.410
While Jim and Pam are having this fight, I thought we should hear it.
当吉姆和帕姆吵架时，我觉得我们应该听听内容。

1228
00:50:49.670 --> 00:50:54.040
You said they were done with the investing and then you volunteered $10,000?
你说过他们不需要投资了，然后你自作主张投了一万美元？

1229
00:50:54.700 --> 00:50:55.680
No, I had to.
不，我必须这么做。

1230
00:50:55.920 --> 00:50:57.420
Look, I needed to look like a team player, Pam.
听着，我得表现得像个团队合作者，帕姆。

1231
00:50:57.580 --> 00:50:59.820
So you invested $10,000 to look like a team player?
所以你为了表现得像个团队合作者就投了一万美元？

1232
00:51:00.140 --> 00:51:09.020
And I love the sumo song.
而且我超爱那首相扑歌。

1233
00:51:24.010 --> 00:51:26.070
Ah, this is a really big fight.
啊，这真的是一场大吵。

1234
00:51:26.150 --> 00:51:29.350
And it's playing out underneath this a cappella song.
而且是在这首阿卡贝拉歌曲的伴奏下进行的。

1235
00:51:29.530 --> 00:51:33.730
But you hear Pam say, wait, that's all of our savings.
但你听到帕姆说，等等，那是我们所有的积蓄。

1236
00:51:34.010 --> 00:51:40.030
First of all, I want to say I'm very impressed that as a newly married couple with two young children,
首先，我想说我印象非常深刻，作为一对有两个年幼孩子的新婚夫妇，

1237
00:51:40.710 --> 00:51:42.430
that they have saved $10,000.
他们竟然存下了一万美元。

1238
00:51:44.130 --> 00:51:45.450
Well done, guys.
干得好，伙计们。

1239
00:51:45.830 --> 00:51:47.190
They clearly, you know.
他们显然，你知道的。

1240
00:51:47.190 --> 00:51:48.470
I've been working at that.
我一直都在为此努力。

1241
00:51:48.570 --> 00:51:51.310
This is something, you know, that doesn't happen by itself.
这可不是随随便便就能做到的。

1242
00:51:51.610 --> 00:51:53.370
And so now it's all gone.
而现在全没了。

1243
00:51:53.710 --> 00:51:53.770
It's gone.
全没了。

1244
00:51:54.190 --> 00:51:56.110
This scene was so much fun to shoot.
这场戏拍得太有趣了。

1245
00:51:56.490 --> 00:51:58.730
I absolutely loved being serenaded.
我绝对喜欢被歌声包围的感觉。

1246
00:51:59.010 --> 00:52:00.930
It was very hard for me to stay angry.
要我保持生气真的很难。

1247
00:52:00.930 --> 00:52:06.930
This is very similar to early in the show when I'm being serenaded by Andy on the banjo,
这和剧集早期我被安迪用班卓琴弹唱时非常相似，

1248
00:52:07.230 --> 00:52:10.550
but I'm supposed to act like I'm annoyed when I love the banjo.
但我得装作很烦的样子，其实我超爱班卓琴。

1249
00:52:10.790 --> 00:52:12.690
So this was very funny.
所以这真的很有趣。

1250
00:52:13.050 --> 00:52:16.670
Well, Nick Caferro shared about this moment in singing to you.
嗯，尼克·卡费罗分享了关于这一刻为你演唱的感受。

1251
00:52:16.870 --> 00:52:17.970
Here's what he had to say.
以下是他要说的话。

1252
00:52:18.190 --> 00:52:24.350
One of the scenes that we did, my biggest scene, was I had to sing I'll Be to Jenna.
我们拍的其中一场戏，也是我最重要的一场戏，就是我得对着珍娜唱《I'll Be》。

1253
00:52:24.750 --> 00:52:28.890
And the first thing was, the conference room was so small.
首先，会议室真的太小了。

1254
00:52:28.930 --> 00:52:29.950
It was so tiny.
非常狭窄。

1255
00:52:30.110 --> 00:52:32.430
I mean, I'm used to seeing it on TV, and I thought it was huge.
我是说，我习惯在电视上看它，以为它很大。

1256
00:52:32.770 --> 00:52:37.510
But to be in there with all of you staring at me was terrifying.
但身处其中，被你们所有人盯着看，真是太可怕了。

1257
00:52:37.990 --> 00:52:41.370
You were like, literally, and I'm not just, again, I'm not just saying this because I'm here.
你们当时真的，我再说一遍，我不是因为在这里才这么说。

1258
00:52:41.530 --> 00:52:42.550
You were all my favorite actors.
你们都是我最喜欢的演员。

1259
00:52:42.610 --> 00:52:43.890
This was my favorite show.
这是我最喜欢的剧。

1260
00:52:44.030 --> 00:52:45.270
And you're all staring at me.
而你们都在盯着我。

1261
00:52:45.350 --> 00:52:46.550
I was so scared.
我当时太紧张了。

1262
00:52:46.750 --> 00:52:51.410
I remember I was on my knees singing to you, I'll be all crying.
我记得我跪在地上为你唱歌，唱着唱着都快哭了。

1263
00:52:51.410 --> 00:52:53.550
And at the end of it, they asked me to kiss your hand.
最后，他们让我亲吻你的手。

1264
00:52:53.670 --> 00:52:56.570
And I was so nervous that, actually, if you go back and watch the episode,
我当时太紧张了，其实如果你回去看那一集的话，

1265
00:52:56.730 --> 00:52:58.590
you'll see I didn't actually kiss your hand.
你会发现我根本没亲到你的手。

1266
00:52:58.730 --> 00:53:03.970
I missed your hand and kissed my thumb, which I get made fun of for a lot.
我亲偏了，亲到了自己的大拇指，这件事我经常被拿来开玩笑。

1267
00:53:04.290 --> 00:53:08.370
There's also a part in that scene, and this made the final cut,
那场戏里还有一个片段，而且被剪进了正片，

1268
00:53:08.990 --> 00:53:12.490
where we did that scene about 20 times.
那场戏我们大概拍了20次。

1269
00:53:13.230 --> 00:53:16.770
Because I remember them saying this is the first time Jim and Pam
因为我记得他们说这是吉姆和帕姆

1270
00:53:16.770 --> 00:53:18.730
have actually gotten to a fight on camera.
第一次在镜头前真正吵架。

1271
00:53:18.770 --> 00:53:19.830
So it was like a big deal.
所以这算是一件大事。

1272
00:53:19.830 --> 00:53:23.690
And the writers were extremely particular about how the fight should sound.
编剧们对吵架的语气非常讲究。

1273
00:53:23.830 --> 00:53:27.150
So they ended up like rewriting it on the spot several different times.
所以他们最后在现场临时改了好几次剧本。

1274
00:53:27.330 --> 00:53:30.950
We did several different versions, which meant I had to keep singing that song,
我们拍了几个不同的版本，这意味着我得不停地唱那首歌，

1275
00:53:31.010 --> 00:53:35.630
which wasn't great for my voice, and probably became progressively worse and worse as we went.
这对我的嗓子不太好，而且随着拍摄进行，我的声音可能越来越差。

1276
00:53:35.950 --> 00:53:39.630
But for the very last take, I remember we had done it so many times.
但拍最后一条的时候，我记得我们已经拍了太多次了。

1277
00:53:39.630 --> 00:53:40.630
And I was just like, you know what?
我就想，管他呢。

1278
00:53:40.770 --> 00:53:41.250
Screw it.
豁出去了。

1279
00:53:41.670 --> 00:53:45.210
And I was singing to you, and you were arguing with Jim while I was singing.
我当时在为你唱歌，而我在唱的时候你正在和吉姆争吵。

1280
00:53:45.210 --> 00:53:49.390
So I took my finger, my index finger, and put it towards your mouth to shush you.
所以我伸出手指，食指，对着你的嘴想让你安静点。

1281
00:53:49.870 --> 00:53:50.910
And you broke.
结果你笑场了。

1282
00:53:51.070 --> 00:53:51.750
You laughed.
你笑了。

1283
00:53:51.990 --> 00:53:53.670
But it was so funny.
但这太搞笑了。

1284
00:53:53.770 --> 00:53:54.410
We were all laughing.
我们都笑了起来。

1285
00:53:54.410 --> 00:53:55.650
I'll never forget that moment.
我永远不会忘记那一刻。

1286
00:53:55.810 --> 00:53:57.490
It was the best of my life.
那是我一生中最美好的时刻。

1287
00:53:57.810 --> 00:54:00.110
And you said that was so brilliant.
你说那简直太天才了。

1288
00:54:00.210 --> 00:54:02.270
And luckily, it made the cut.
幸运的是，这一幕被保留了下来。

1289
00:54:02.430 --> 00:54:06.070
You see in the video me raising my finger to shush you.
你在视频里能看到我举起手指让你安静。

1290
00:54:06.290 --> 00:54:07.410
But yeah, that was so fun.
总之，那真的太有趣了。

1291
00:54:07.410 --> 00:54:08.710
And that's something I'll never forget.
那是我永远不会忘记的事情。

1292
00:54:09.950 --> 00:54:11.910
So, lady, I remember when he did that.
所以，女士，我记得他做那个动作的时候。

1293
00:54:12.110 --> 00:54:15.310
I remember when he put his finger up to my face to shush me.
我记得他把手指伸到我脸上让我安静的时候。

1294
00:54:15.510 --> 00:54:19.270
I can't believe we had enough footage to keep it in the episode,
真不敢相信我们有足够的素材把它保留在剧集里，

1295
00:54:19.270 --> 00:54:23.610
because I felt like I immediately broke, because I thought that was so funny.
因为我觉得我当时立刻就笑场了，因为我觉得那太搞笑了。

1296
00:54:23.990 --> 00:54:29.770
But the whole thing was like, he was so earnestly, sweetly singing right in my face.
但整件事就是，他那么真诚、那么甜美地对着我的脸唱歌。

1297
00:54:29.950 --> 00:54:30.090
Yeah.
没错。

1298
00:54:30.330 --> 00:54:32.650
It was hard to keep a straight face the whole time.
全程忍住不笑真的很难。

1299
00:54:33.090 --> 00:54:35.250
You know, after we filmed this conference room scene,
你知道，拍完这场会议室的戏后，

1300
00:54:35.250 --> 00:54:39.450
Nick shared that he had a very interesting encounter with Rainn Wilson.
尼克分享说他与雷恩·威尔森有过一次非常有趣的邂逅。

1301
00:54:39.670 --> 00:54:39.970
Yeah.
没错。

1302
00:54:40.270 --> 00:54:41.930
He sent in an audio clip about it.
他发来了一段关于这件事的音频。

1303
00:54:42.050 --> 00:54:47.110
I want you to hear it, because Rainn was not the curmudgeon we know him to be.
我想让你们听听，因为雷恩并不是我们所熟知的那种脾气暴躁的人。

1304
00:54:47.310 --> 00:54:49.730
He was the other part of Rainn.
那是雷恩的另一面。

1305
00:54:49.890 --> 00:54:51.870
He was, and he changed Nick's life.
确实如此，而且他改变了尼克的人生。

1306
00:54:51.870 --> 00:54:52.310
He did.
他确实改变了。

1307
00:54:52.470 --> 00:54:53.170
Here's the clip.
音频就在这儿。

1308
00:54:53.850 --> 00:54:59.490
Another moment I'll never forget, and actually had a huge impact on my life and my life trajectory,
另一个我永远不会忘记的时刻，它实际上对我的人生和职业轨迹产生了巨大的影响，

1309
00:55:01.410 --> 00:55:06.470
was after the conference room scene, or during the conference room scene, in between takes,
是在会议室那场戏之后，或者说在拍摄会议室那场戏的间隙，

1310
00:55:06.930 --> 00:55:11.410
Rainn Wilson was sitting right next to where me and my a cappella group were standing,
雷恩·威尔森当时就坐在我和我的阿卡贝拉合唱团成员站的地方旁边，

1311
00:55:11.410 --> 00:55:15.570
and he started a conversation, and he said, hey, so are you guys actors?
他主动开启了话题，他说，嘿，你们是演员吗？

1312
00:55:16.150 --> 00:55:19.490
And we were like, no, we're from University of Virginia.
我们当时回答说，不是，我们来自弗吉尼亚大学。

1313
00:55:19.490 --> 00:55:22.170
We're just here, you know, to play the a cappella group.
我们来这儿只是为了，你知道，扮演那个阿卡贝拉合唱团。

1314
00:55:22.310 --> 00:55:23.510
We're a cappella group singers.
我们是阿卡贝拉合唱团的歌手。

1315
00:55:24.110 --> 00:55:26.950
And he pointed to me, and he said, you should be an actor.
然后他指着我说，你应该当演员。

1316
00:55:27.170 --> 00:55:29.590
You should consider doing this.
你应该考虑从事这一行。

1317
00:55:30.410 --> 00:55:34.010
And this was after I had a scene with a few lines and sang.
那是在我演完一场有几句台词并唱了歌的戏之后。

1318
00:55:34.250 --> 00:55:40.910
And I was like so starstruck and taken aback by that, but it really meant a lot to me,
我当时又惊又喜，完全没想到他会这么说，但这对我来说意义重大，

1319
00:55:40.910 --> 00:55:49.150
and truly is one of the reasons I decided to move out to Los Angeles after I graduated
这确实是我毕业后决定搬到洛杉矶的原因之一，

1320
00:55:49.150 --> 00:55:51.270
and to pursue this career.
也是我决定追求这份事业的原因。

1321
00:55:51.270 --> 00:55:57.170
So thank you to Rainn Wilson for saying that to me and for giving me a vote of confidence,
所以感谢雷恩·威尔森对我说了那番话，并给了我一份信任票，

1322
00:55:57.170 --> 00:56:02.470
and you've really had a big impact on my life, and I hope that I get to meet him again one day
你真的对我的人生影响深远，我希望有一天能再次见到他，

1323
00:56:02.470 --> 00:56:05.330
so I can thank him in person, because it really meant a lot to me.
这样我就能当面感谢他，因为那对我来说真的意义非凡。

1324
00:56:06.270 --> 00:56:07.310
So there you go.
所以，就是这样。

1325
00:56:07.490 --> 00:56:11.010
Nick had his Molly Shannon moment with Rainn.
尼克在雷恩身上找到了他自己的莫莉·香农时刻。

1326
00:56:11.090 --> 00:56:11.770
Oh, yes.
噢，没错。

1327
00:56:11.870 --> 00:56:14.910
This is your Molly Shannon moment where she told you to stick with it.
这就是你的莫莉·香农时刻，当时她也告诉你要坚持下去。

1328
00:56:15.030 --> 00:56:15.270
Yes.
是的。

1329
00:56:15.410 --> 00:56:17.310
I met her right when I first got to L.A.
我刚到洛杉矶时就遇到了她。

1330
00:56:17.310 --> 00:56:20.310
And so Nick took Rainn's advice.
所以尼克听取了雷恩的建议。

1331
00:56:20.370 --> 00:56:21.710
He moved to L.A.
他搬到了洛杉矶。

1332
00:56:22.090 --> 00:56:23.610
He's been in a bunch of commercials.
他拍过很多广告。

1333
00:56:23.610 --> 00:56:28.390
He's been on Blackish and 9-1-1, and he is currently in the Sunday company at Groundlings.
他出演过《喜新不厌旧》和《紧急呼救》，目前是Groundlings剧团周日演出组的成员。

1334
00:56:28.710 --> 00:56:32.990
He's also teamed up with Halstead again and Claire again on different projects.
他还与哈尔斯特德和克莱尔在不同的项目中再次合作过。

1335
00:56:32.990 --> 00:56:34.530
He's now a working actor.
他现在是一名职业演员了。

1336
00:56:34.530 --> 00:56:35.650
This is so crazy.
这真是太疯狂了。

1337
00:56:35.650 --> 00:56:41.090
All from this, like, random email that he got one day he was in college.
这一切都源于他在大学时偶然收到的一封邮件。

1338
00:56:41.470 --> 00:56:48.710
You know, Nick's in one last clip for us, you guys, and it's about, well, it's about things you learn on set.
大家注意，尼克还有最后一段音频要分享，是关于，嗯，关于在片场学到的东西。

1339
00:56:48.990 --> 00:56:58.650
And one of the guys in the a cappella group learned that, well, he didn't understand how the toilet worked in the trailer that they were using.
合唱团里的一个人学到了，嗯，他当时搞不懂他们用的拖车里的厕所是怎么运作的。

1340
00:57:00.370 --> 00:57:02.410
And I think for anyone coming to L.A.
我觉得对于任何来到洛杉矶

1341
00:57:02.470 --> 00:57:06.090
who wants to be an actor, this is an important lesson to learn.
想要成为演员的人来说，这是一个很重要的教训。

1342
00:57:06.270 --> 00:57:06.770
Let's hear it.
我们来听听吧。

1343
00:57:07.310 --> 00:57:07.710
Okay.
好的。

1344
00:57:07.810 --> 00:57:14.390
So this story is one that you would probably never share, but I have to tell you because it's just too outrageous to not.
这个故事你可能永远不会分享，但我必须告诉你，因为它实在太离谱了，不得不说。

1345
00:57:15.410 --> 00:57:17.110
When we were there, there were eight of us.
我们当时在那儿，一共八个人。

1346
00:57:17.210 --> 00:57:22.470
And so we all got trailers on set, and we shared them with each other, these little honey wagons.
我们在片场都分到了拖车，我们互相共用这些小型的移动化妆间。

1347
00:57:22.770 --> 00:57:24.670
There were two per each trailer.
每辆拖车里有两个人。

1348
00:57:24.670 --> 00:57:26.150
And the trailers are small.
拖车很小。

1349
00:57:26.290 --> 00:57:31.530
They have, like, a little couch and, you know, a little closet to put your costumes in and a tiny little bathroom.
里面有个小沙发，你知道，还有个小衣柜用来放戏服，以及一个极小的洗手间。

1350
00:57:32.330 --> 00:57:42.270
And I remember I shared my trailer with one of my fellow a cappella group members whose name I will not mention for reasons that will soon become obvious.
我记得我和我的一位合唱团成员共用一辆拖车，出于显而易见的原因，我就不提他的名字了。

1351
00:57:42.590 --> 00:57:44.450
And I remember he was in the trailer.
我记得当时他在拖车里。

1352
00:57:44.450 --> 00:57:46.510
I was going to go get fitted.
我正要去试装。

1353
00:57:46.630 --> 00:57:50.230
When my fitting was done, I came back to walk up the stairs to our trailer.
试装结束后，我回来准备走上台阶回到我们的拖车。

1354
00:57:50.230 --> 00:57:59.070
And as I did, he burst through the door carrying a giant wad of paper towels and kind of, like, rushing down the stairs past me.
就在这时，他冲出门来，手里抓着一大团纸巾，急匆匆地从我身边跑下台阶。

1355
00:57:59.570 --> 00:58:01.130
And I was like, okay, that's strange.
我当时心想，好吧，这真奇怪。

1356
00:58:01.130 --> 00:58:03.410
And he went and threw them in a trash can.
然后他走过去把纸巾扔进了垃圾桶。

1357
00:58:03.510 --> 00:58:04.850
I was like, okay, cool.
我心想，好吧，行吧。

1358
00:58:05.010 --> 00:58:05.910
That was a lot of paper towels.
那纸巾也太多了。

1359
00:58:06.110 --> 00:58:07.190
I get back in the trailer.
我回到拖车里。

1360
00:58:07.350 --> 00:58:07.950
I'm sitting there.
我坐在那儿。

1361
00:58:08.070 --> 00:58:08.750
He comes in.
他进来了。

1362
00:58:09.090 --> 00:58:11.570
And I'm like, oh, it smells off in here.
我说，噢，这儿味道有点不对劲。

1363
00:58:12.330 --> 00:58:16.110
Did you, like, you know, pass gas or use the bathroom?
你是不是，你知道的，放屁了还是上厕所了？

1364
00:58:16.210 --> 00:58:17.210
And he was like, no, no, no, no.
他说，没有，没有，没有，没有。

1365
00:58:17.210 --> 00:58:18.670
And I was like, dude, are you sure?
我说，老兄，你确定吗？

1366
00:58:18.790 --> 00:58:22.930
Like, it smells like somebody went to the bathroom and took a poop.
闻起来就像有人上过厕所，拉了屎一样。

1367
00:58:23.050 --> 00:58:23.910
And I was like, are you sure?
我说，你确定吗？

1368
00:58:24.070 --> 00:58:25.870
He's like, okay, yes, I did.
他说，好吧，是的，我确实上了。

1369
00:58:26.070 --> 00:58:28.210
I used, went to the bathroom and the toilet.
我用了，去了厕所，用了马桶。

1370
00:58:28.430 --> 00:58:30.050
And I, it doesn't work.
然后我，它坏了。

1371
00:58:30.130 --> 00:58:30.870
It doesn't flush.
冲不了水。

1372
00:58:31.250 --> 00:58:36.530
So I had to take all the paper towels and pick it up and throw it out in the trash.
所以我只好拿了所有的纸巾，把它捡起来扔进了垃圾桶。

1373
00:58:36.970 --> 00:58:39.250
And I was like, oh, my God.
我当时心想，天哪。

1374
00:58:39.670 --> 00:58:40.910
Are you kidding me?
你在开玩笑吗？

1375
00:58:41.210 --> 00:58:45.210
It turned out the toilet was one of the ones that had a foot pedal.
原来那个马桶是那种带脚踏板的。

1376
00:58:45.210 --> 00:58:49.310
There's a pedal underneath the toilet that you push down with your foot and it flushes.
马桶下面有个踏板，你用脚踩下去就能冲水。

1377
00:58:49.430 --> 00:58:51.410
And he didn't know that and couldn't find it.
他不知道这一点，也没找到踏板。

1378
00:58:51.510 --> 00:58:53.390
He just thought it was a broken toilet.
他以为马桶坏了。

1379
00:58:53.590 --> 00:59:00.050
So he panicked, wrapped his hands in paper towels, and picked up his own mess, ran it
所以他慌了，用纸巾包住手，捡起自己的排泄物，跑出

1380
00:59:00.050 --> 00:59:03.850
through the door, and threw it away in a trash can.
门外，把它扔进了垃圾桶。

1381
00:59:05.310 --> 00:59:08.030
I was mortified to hear this.
听到这些我简直尴尬得要死。

1382
00:59:08.110 --> 00:59:11.210
I have never heard of more unhinged behavior.
我从来没听过这么离谱的行为。

1383
00:59:11.750 --> 00:59:14.110
I was like, dude, it's just a foot pedal.
我说，老兄，那只是个脚踏板而已。

1384
00:59:14.110 --> 00:59:16.450
You have ruined Dunder Mifflin.
你把邓德·米夫林公司给毁了。

1385
00:59:16.830 --> 00:59:24.670
This is, so, yeah, to anybody who emptied the trash over there, I apologize on his behalf.
所以，是的，对于任何清理过那边垃圾的人，我代他向你们道歉。

